# API Source of Truth — Live Postman Collection

Backend and Flutter are developed in parallel. The Postman Collection is a **living API contract**. Endpoints, payloads, fields, validation, and behavior may change between tasks.

## Collection

- Workspace: [InsurFlow Postman Collection](https://www.postman.com/mohammedferwana2-211262/mohammed-ferwana-s-workspace/collection/pace502/insurflow?sideView=agentMode)
- Default base URL: `https://insurflow-backend.onrender.com/api/v1`
- Configure the URL only in `lib/core/config/app_config.dart` (`API_BASE_URL` dart-define). Never hardcode it in features.

## Before every task

Before implementing **any** feature, screen, flow, model, repository, BLoC/Cubit, or change that uses backend data:

1. Understand the screen, required data, user actions, fetch/submit/update needs.
2. Fetch/inspect the **current** Postman Collection (not memory, not prior chats, not existing Dart models).
3. Search for related endpoints: method, path, params, headers, auth, body, multipart, responses, errors, status codes, pagination, status values.
4. Compare with existing Flutter code. Integrate new/changed APIs automatically; never invent missing ones.

Do **not** rely on previous conversations, local models, old services, or cached endpoint assumptions.

## Never invent

- Do not invent endpoints, routes, query params, or response fields.
- If the collection is incomplete, treat missing APIs as not ready — do not guess.
- When an existing Flutter API differs from Postman (path, method, body, fields, nullability, statuses), **update Flutter to match Postman**.
